D {"e":"workflow","a":"neuroplast-loop","b":"Neuroplast execution loop","c":"Declarative description of the Neuroplast working loop.","x":true,"ah":[{"a":"conceptualize","b":"Conceptualize","c":"Frame or reframe the work against the durable project mind."},{"a":"plan","b":"Plan","c":"Produce a bounded, resumable plan under neuroplast/plans/."},{"a":"act","b":"Act","c":"Execute one bounded step, reading assembled context and respecting the contract."},{"a":"changelog","b":"Changelog","c":"Record the completed cycle and keep user-facing docs in sync."},{"a":"think","b":"Think","c":"Capture durable learnings as LCP memory entries via write-back, then regenerate the pack and distilled quantized indexes for the next cycle."}],"h":{"g":"."},"d":"2026-06-30T12:00:00Z"}
D {"e":"rule","a":"neuroplast-boundaries","b":"Neuroplast implementation boundaries","c":"Boundaries that keep Neuroplast aligned with LCP.","l":[{"a":"lcp-protocol","r":"https://github.com/JamesNapoletano/lcp","e":"protocol","m":"depends_on"}],"ai":"Neuroplast is an LCP operational layer; it must read assembled context and write durable memory back as ordinary LCP knowledge entries without redefining the core protocol.","ae":"Keeping Neuroplast a conformant consumer of LCP preserves portability and lets any other consumer interpret the same files.","ag":"error","af":["Neuroplast must reference the official LCP repository as the normative protocol source.","Neuroplast must not claim to define LCP independently.","Durable memory must be recorded as LCP knowledge entries with provenance, never as opaque runtime state."],"h":{"g":"."},"d":"2026-06-30T12:00:00Z"}
D {"e":"reasoning_scaffold","a":"neuroplast-execution-scaffold","b":"Neuroplast execution scaffold","c":"Explicit scaffold for carrying out bounded work while preserving durable context.","t":["Assemble the working context view from the distilled high-signal index (active profile, scope, intent).","Update the active plan.","Execute the bounded work.","Record changelog updates.","Write durable learnings back as LCP memory entries.","Regenerate the lossless (pack) and high-signal (distill) quantized indexes so the next cycle assembles current memory."],"w":["Read assembled context before acting; treat the view as derived and disposable.","Keep memory explicit and inspectable; supersede rather than overwrite.","Quantize after write-back; distill applies the memory lifecycle so retired and low-confidence entries do not re-enter the loaded context."],"h":{"g":"."},"d":"2026-06-30T12:00:00Z"}
D {"e":"tool_description","a":"neuroplast-cli","b":"Neuroplast CLI","c":"Tooling for initializing, syncing, validating, and quantizing Neuroplast repositories.","aa":["a target repository root","an interaction-routing phrase (for route)"],"ac":["scaffolded and refreshed managed files (init, sync)","a validation report against the LCP v2.0 schemas (validate)","a derived .lcp/indexes/context.lcpq bundle (quantize)"],"u":["init","sync","validate","route","quantize"],"v":["The .lcpq bundle is derived; the source .lcp documents remain authoritative.","Consumer-owned knowledge memory is never overwritten by sync.","The tool describes a local utility and is not an invocation protocol."],"h":{"g":"."},"d":"2026-06-30T00:00:00Z"}
D {"e":"knowledge_artifact","a":"neuroplast-compatibility","b":"Neuroplast compatibility knowledge","c":"How Neuroplast fits inside LCP while preserving its own defaults.","n":"compatibility","o":[{"a":"neuroplast-implements-lcp","k":"active","i":1,"j":"Neuroplast is an implementation (operational layer) of LCP.","d":"2026-06-30T00:00:00Z"},{"a":"neuroplast-owns-working-layout","k":"active","i":1,"j":"Neuroplast preserves /neuroplast/ as its implementation-owned working layout, while .lcp/ holds the portable LCP context.","d":"2026-06-30T00:00:00Z"},{"a":"neuroplast-binds-operationally","k":"active","i":1,"j":"Neuroplast reads assembled context views and writes durable memory back as LCP knowledge entries, per the operational-binding extension.","d":"2026-06-30T00:00:00Z"}],"h":{"g":"."},"d":"2026-06-30T00:00:00Z"}
D {"e":"knowledge_artifact","a":"neuroplast-learning","b":"Neuroplast durable learning memory","c":"Durable, reusable learnings captured during Neuroplast work cycles. This is the sole source of truth for memory; there is no separate rendered view.","n":"learning","o":[{"a":"ui-layout-patterns","k":"active","i":0.8,"b":"UI Layout Patterns","j":"## Stacked reference workspaces over nested editor grids\n- When a non-writing workspace contains multiple related editors, prefer a single surface-level title card followed by a table of contents and anchored collapsible sections.\n- This keeps page identity stable while still letting operators jump directly to the correct editor block.\n- Reuse one shared section scaffold across surfaces so single-editor and multi-editor workspaces feel like the same product system.\n- Hide the table of contents when the shared surface exposes fewer than two sections so single-editor pages avoid redundant navigation chrome.\n- Do not repeat the section title inside the expanded body card unless the body is introducing a distinct nested sub-area; otherwise the accordion header should carry the naming burden alone.","d":"2026-07-02T14:02:58Z"}],"h":{"g":"."},"d":"2026-07-02T14:04:55Z"}
